      "content": "Given your age and the immediate symptoms of fainting and dizziness, waiting and ignoring this is not advisable even if you feel better now. The risk of sudden cardiac events or severe dehydration-related complications is high enough that you should make an appointment with your family doctor as soon as possible, ideally within a day or two, to get advice that fits your schedule and concerns. Avoid driving or playing sports until you have been evaluated by a professional.",
      "source": "target",
